1
00:00:12,200 --> 00:00:14,400
Good evening, Georgia.
晚上好，佐治亚州。

2
00:00:18,320 --> 00:00:27,910
Over the last year and a half, we have traveled from the red hills of Georgia to the Blue Ridge mountains of the Piedmont.
在过去的一年半里，我们从佐治亚州的红山到皮埃蒙特的蓝岭山脉。

3
00:00:27,910 --> 00:00:31,240
From the coastal shores to rolling farmlands.
从沿海海岸到连绵起伏的农田。

4
00:00:32,040 --> 00:00:34,800
From urban streets to rural communities.
从城市街道到农村社区。

5
00:00:35,300 --> 00:00:43,900
And with each stop, your faces, your families, your communities, your hopes and your dreams,
每到一站，你们的面孔、你们的家人、你们的社区、你们的希望和你们的梦想，

6
00:00:43,900 --> 00:00:49,060
And even your disappointments have been imprinted upon my heart.
甚至你的失望也铭刻在我的心上。

7
00:00:56,840 --> 00:01:03,200
This campaign was about every community in every corner of Georgia.
这项活动涉及佐治亚州每个角落的每个社区。

8
00:01:05,060 --> 00:01:09,080
It is for the veteran who needs access to health care.
它适用于需要获得医疗保健的退伍军人。

9
00:01:11,230 --> 00:01:17,510
It's for the college student who wonders if the cost of their education is worth it.
它适合那些想知道他们的教育费用是否值得的大学生。

10
00:01:18,590 --> 00:01:23,650
It is for the teenager who's asked about mental health support.
这是为被询问心理健康支持的青少年准备的。

11
00:01:24,750 --> 00:01:34,230
This win is for the caregiver who can't afford health care and needs Georgia to finally expand Medicaid.
这场胜利是为那些无力承担医疗保健并需要佐治亚州最终扩大医疗补助的护理人员赢得的。

12
00:01:39,460 --> 00:01:44,600
It is for the entrepreneur who is seeking to grow her small business.
它适合寻求发展小型企业的企业家。

13
00:01:45,456 --> 00:01:53,320
This win is for the farmer who is trying to hold on to his family land.
这场胜利属于试图保住家庭土地的农民。

14
00:01:53,960 --> 00:02:00,240
It is for the teacher who's working two jobs so that they can educate our children.
它是为那些同时做两份工作的老师准备的，这样他们就可以教育我们的孩子。

15
00:02:02,120 --> 00:02:08,580
And this win is for the child who deserves every opportunity to succeed.
这场胜利是属于那些值得拥有一切成功机会的孩子的。

16
00:02:10,840 --> 00:02:15,040
Georgia, this win is for all of us.
佐治亚州，这场胜利属于我们所有人。

17
00:02:19,570 --> 00:02:20,390
Thank you, Georgia.
谢谢你，佐治亚州。

18
00:02:21,010 --> 00:02:24,490
I am honored to be your 84th governor.
我很荣幸成为你们的第 84 任州长。

19
00:02:40,580 --> 00:02:43,920
I spoke with Rick Jackson just a while ago.
不久前我和里克·杰克逊谈过。

20
00:02:44,260 --> 00:02:53,593
And I thanked him for a hard-fought race.
我感谢他带来了一场艰苦的比赛。

21
00:02:53,593 --> 00:03:00,920
And we agreed that together we would continue to support foster children across this state.
我们一致同意，我们将共同继续支持全州的寄养儿童。

22
00:03:04,480 --> 00:03:11,950
And no matter who you voted for tonight, I will be a governor for all of Georgia.
无论你今晚投票给谁，我都将成为整个佐治亚州的州长。

23
00:03:16,540 --> 00:03:23,700
From the beginning of this campaign, I believed that God would not give vision without provision.
从这次活动一开始，我就相信上帝不会在没有供应的情况下赐予异象。

24
00:03:25,292 --> 00:03:30,913
That provision has come by the way of every prayer sent, every door knocked,
这个供应是通过每一次祈祷、每一次敲门来实现的，

25
00:03:30,940 --> 00:03:37,700
Every phone call made, and every donation given, and every sign that has been planted.
每打一个电话，每一次捐款，每一个标语。

26
00:03:38,440 --> 00:03:47,650
In big and small ways, you've shown that no amount of money will ever Never,
你在大大小小的方面都表明，再多的钱也永远不会，

27
00:03:48,668 --> 00:03:54,774
Ever, ever overcome the power of the people.
永远、永远战胜人民的力量。

28
00:03:55,802 --> 00:04:03,670
To Derrick, you are my rock and the love of my life.
对于德里克来说，你是我的磐石，也是我一生的挚爱。

29
00:04:06,710 --> 00:04:08,910
And I am grateful to be your wife.
我很感激能成为你的妻子。

30
00:04:10,690 --> 00:04:14,250
Lance, Langston, Lennox, and Lincoln.
兰斯、兰斯顿、伦诺克斯和林肯。

31
00:04:14,890 --> 00:04:19,570
The highest honor I will ever have is to be your mother.
我一生中最高的荣誉就是成为你的母亲。

32
00:04:21,980 --> 00:04:24,200
Mama, you are the real mvp.
妈妈，你才是真正的mvp。

33
00:04:28,894 --> 00:04:34,350
And you told me that God was going to show himself at his finest today.
你告诉我上帝今天将展现他最好的一面。

34
00:04:34,910 --> 00:04:38,910
And our God has exceeded all of my expectations.
我们的神超出了我所有的期望。

35
00:04:43,010 --> 00:04:49,564
To my big sister Tracy and my brother Darian.
致我的姐姐特雷西和我的弟弟达里安。

36
00:04:49,610 --> 00:04:56,910
All of my siblings, all of my family, and my dearest friends, I am eternally grateful for you.
我所有的兄弟姐妹，我所有的家人，还有我最亲爱的朋友，我永远感激你们。

37
00:04:57,974 --> 00:04:59,531
And to my daddy.
还有我的爸爸。

38
00:05:03,920 --> 00:05:14,600
Thank you, daddy, for your unconditional love and for instilling in me a fearlessness that made me believe that I could be and do
爸爸，谢谢您无条件的爱，并给我灌输了无所畏惧的精神，让我相信我可以做到。

39
00:05:14,600 --> 00:05:16,200
Whatever my heart desired.
随心所欲。

40
00:05:17,023 --> 00:05:25,860
Grandmama, granddaddy, other mama, and the rest of the great heavenly cloud of witnesses.
奶奶、爷爷、其他妈妈，以及其他伟大的天上见证人云彩。

41
00:05:26,974 --> 00:05:33,200
We have run this way race with perseverance and I know you cheered us on the entire way.
我们坚持不懈地跑完了这条路，我知道你们全程为我们加油。

42
00:05:34,760 --> 00:05:39,656
Sharon Hickson, Rashad Taylor, Darian Johnson.
莎朗·希克森、拉沙德·泰勒、达里安·约翰逊。

43
00:05:43,737 --> 00:05:47,170
The golden three-legged stool is undefeated.
黄金三足凳不败。

44
00:05:47,470 --> 00:05:58,310
And the entire team klb, I wish I had time to call all your names.
还有 klb 整个团队，我希望我有时间叫出你们所有人的名字。

45
00:05:59,323 --> 00:06:01,590
I love and appreciate you all.
我爱并感谢你们所有人。

46
00:06:01,770 --> 00:06:04,630
Tonight I love you, too.
今晚我也爱你。

47
00:06:06,330 --> 00:06:12,410
Tonight would not have been possible without your long hours and your sacrifices.
如果没有你们长时间的工作和牺牲，今晚就不可能实现。

48
00:06:13,270 --> 00:06:19,510
And to the volunteers who committed so much of your own lives to this effort, Thank you.
感谢那些为这项工作奉献了自己一生的志愿者们，谢谢你。

49
00:06:19,904 --> 00:06:26,490
Your never-ending belief in this campaign has made today a reality.
你们对这场运动永不停歇的信念使今天成为了现实。

50
00:06:26,970 --> 00:06:32,270
You sent a message that will ring across our state and our nation.
您发出的信息将响彻我们州和本州。

51
00:06:33,110 --> 00:06:46,094
You voted and you voted with whole ballot energy and we have reelected my friend and our senator Jon Ossoff.
你们投票了，你们用全部选票的能量投票了，我们再次选举了我的朋友和我们的参议员乔恩·奥索夫。

52
00:06:47,789 --> 00:06:56,600
And with Jon Ossoff and my friend and my senator and our senator Raphael Warnock,
和乔恩·奥索夫、我的朋友、我的参议员和我们的参议员拉斐尔·沃诺克一起，

53
00:06:56,780 --> 00:07:03,470
We are blessed to have two senators who make Georgia proud.
我们很幸运有两位让佐治亚州感到自豪的参议员。

54
00:07:05,550 --> 00:07:10,770
Yesterday I had the opportunity to visit Crawfordville, Georgia.
昨天我有机会访问了佐治亚州克劳福德维尔。

55
00:07:11,495 --> 00:07:16,510
The town where my family traces its roots at least five generations.
我的家族至少有五代人在这个小镇扎根。

56
00:07:17,330 --> 00:07:29,605
It was the town that was home to the former governor of Georgia and the vice president of the Confederate States of America, Alexander Stephens.
这是佐治亚州前州长和美利坚联盟国副总统的家乡。亚历山大·斯蒂芬斯.

57
00:07:29,605 --> 00:07:36,710
I visited the grave of Betsy Peak, my great-great-grandmother, who was born in 1845,
我参观了我的曾曾祖母贝特西·皮克 (Betsy Peak) 的坟墓，她出生于 1845 年，

58
00:07:37,070 --> 00:07:39,830
20 years before emancipation.
距离解放还有20年。

59
00:07:40,615 --> 00:07:45,510
In a cemetery filled with unmarked graves, I found hers.
在一片没有标记的坟墓的墓地里，我找到了她的坟墓。

60
00:07:46,510 --> 00:07:54,970
I don't know what dreams Betsy Peak had for her children or for her grandchildren or the generations that she would never meet,
我不知道贝特西·皮克对她的孩子、她的孙子或她永远不会见到的几代人有什么梦想，

61
00:07:55,570 --> 00:07:59,130
But I know I am standing on shoulders made of steel.
但我知道我站在钢铁的肩膀上。

62
00:08:00,120 --> 00:08:13,650
So, yes, Crawfordville produced the Confederacy's vice president, but tonight it also produced your next governor.
所以，是的，克劳福德维尔产生了联邦副总统，但今晚它也产生了你们的下一任州长。

63
00:08:18,610 --> 00:08:23,430
Tonight should remind us all that no matter what community we come from,
今晚应该提醒我们所有人，无论我们来自哪个社区，

64
00:08:23,670 --> 00:08:29,130
Georgia is not defined by one moment in time or by one person.
佐治亚州不是由某一时刻或某个人定义的。

65
00:08:29,790 --> 00:08:36,790
It's been defined by all of us, and I will be a governor for everyone in this state.
它是由我们所有人定义的，我将成为本州每个人的州长。

66
00:08:39,170 --> 00:08:51,750
Georgia, we sent a message loud and clear that we want a leader who will put Georgia first and who will stand up to
佐治亚州，我们大声而明确地发出了一个信息，我们想要一位将佐治亚州放在首位并且能够挺身而出的领导人

67
00:08:51,750 --> 00:08:55,130
All the chaos coming out of Washington, D.C.
所有的混乱都来自华盛顿特区

68
00:08:55,796 --> 00:09:04,360
But even more importantly, you sent the message that in these times of division and acrimony,
但更重要的是，你传达的信息是，在这个分裂和尖酸刻薄的时代，

69
00:09:04,600 --> 00:09:06,980
You believe in something foundational.
你相信一些基本的东西。

70
00:09:07,540 --> 00:09:08,960
And that is hope.
这就是希望。

71
00:09:09,700 --> 00:09:14,940
And that is why we launched this campaign 532 days ago.
这就是我们在 532 天前发起这项活动的原因。

72
00:09:15,840 --> 00:09:20,180
Over the last year and a half, I've had the privilege of traveling across Georgia,
在过去的一年半里，我有幸穿越了佐治亚州，

73
00:09:20,780 --> 00:09:32,080
Talking with people, listening to their concerns, and hearing how excited Georgians are to have a chance at something better for their families and For their communities.
与人们交谈，倾听他们的担忧，并听到佐治亚州人为有机会为家人和朋友谋求更好的生活而感到多么兴奋为了他们的社区。

74
00:09:32,860 --> 00:09:40,900
Those conversations anchored our campaign because this campaign has always been about the people we serve.
这些对话奠定了我们的竞选活动的基础，因为这场竞选活动始终以我们服务的人民​​为中心。

75
00:09:41,680 --> 00:09:48,060
It's about everyday hardworking people who want to be able to afford to put food on the table,
这是关于那些每天努力工作的人们，他们希望能够养家糊口，

76
00:09:48,560 --> 00:09:51,560
To give our children the opportunities they deserve.
为我们的孩子提供他们应得的机会。

77
00:09:51,560 --> 00:09:56,500
It's about making sure our seniors can age in place with dignity.
这是为了确保我们的老年人能够有尊严地安享晚年。

78
00:09:57,300 --> 00:10:02,620
It's about ensuring that our veterans can receive the health care that they have earned.
这是为了确保我们的退伍军人能够获得他们应得的医疗保健。

79
00:10:03,560 --> 00:10:09,760
This campaign is about making sure that every Georgian, no matter their background,
这项运动旨在确保每个佐治亚州人，无论其背景如何，

80
00:10:09,760 --> 00:10:13,680
Their zip code, has a fair chance at building a better future.
他们的邮政编码有公平的机会建设更美好的未来。

81
00:10:14,420 --> 00:10:18,980
And that is what I will fight for every day as your governor.
这就是我作为你们的州长每天为之奋斗的目标。

82
00:10:20,292 --> 00:10:25,910
This has been a long campaign.
这是一场漫长的竞选活动。

83
00:10:27,610 --> 00:10:33,250
And there are many days that weren't easy, and there were a lot of tough decisions to make.
有很多日子并不轻松，需要做出很多艰难的决定。

84
00:10:34,150 --> 00:10:41,008
But my faith has reminded me that we are never to grow weary in well-doing.
但我的信仰提醒我，我们永远不要厌倦行善。

85
00:10:41,018 --> 00:10:50,230
From Congressman John Lewis, who didn't let batons and billy clubs stop him from demanding that everyone be included in our democracy,
来自国会议员约翰·刘易斯，他没有让警棍和警棍阻止他要求每个人都参与我们的民主，

86
00:10:50,808 --> 00:11:00,130
To my aunt Ruby Doris Smith Robinson, who organized the first sit-ins with students at the Atlanta University Center,
我的阿姨鲁比·多丽丝·史密斯·罗宾逊在亚特兰大大学中心组织了第一次学生静坐，

87
00:11:00,190 --> 00:11:10,730
And to our native son President Jimmy Carter, who made sure that Georgia invested in every school across this country,
感谢我们的儿子吉米·卡特总统，他确保佐治亚州投资于全国每所学校，

88
00:11:10,950 --> 00:11:16,530
Across our state, and even established the Department of Education.
我们全州，甚至设立了教育部。

89
00:11:17,630 --> 00:11:24,970
So, Georgia has always been a state where we didn't settle for what was before us,
所以，佐治亚州一直是一个我们不满足于眼前的事情的州，

90
00:11:25,190 --> 00:11:27,870
But we have always fought for better.
但我们一直在为更好的目标而奋斗。

91
00:11:28,858 --> 00:11:34,490
In acts big and small, we all have the ability to shape our future.
通过大大小小的行动，我们都有能力塑造我们的未来。

92
00:11:35,110 --> 00:11:38,430
That is the legacy that we have in Georgia.
这就是我们在佐治亚州所拥有的遗产。

93
00:11:38,990 --> 00:11:48,050
It's a legacy that comes with responsibility, and it is that responsibility that I will take to the governor's office.
这是一种伴随着责任的遗产，而我将把这种责任带到州长办公室。

94
00:11:49,373 --> 00:12:01,650
I've had a chance to think about not just the path ahead, but the path that we've traveled and the stories I've heard.
我有机会思考的不仅是前方的道路，还有我们走过的道路和我听到的故事。

95
00:12:02,370 --> 00:12:08,290
From the woman in Columbus who owns a child care center because she wants to nurture the next generation,
来自哥伦布的一位女士，她拥有一家儿童保育中心，因为她想培育下一代，

96
00:12:08,850 --> 00:12:13,990
To the woman I met in Atlanta who owns a mobile mammogram clinic,
对于我在亚特兰大遇到的一位拥有移动乳房X光检查诊所的女士，

97
00:12:14,370 --> 00:12:18,890
Who had her funding completely cut with guts to the cdc.
她的资金完全被削减了，她对疾控中心有勇气。

98
00:12:20,139 --> 00:12:25,030
I think about the veteran I met in Augusta who wants support for that small business,
我想起我在奥古斯塔遇到的一位退伍军人，他希望为那家小企业提供支持，

99
00:12:25,030 --> 00:12:29,850
And the teacher in Waycross who's working two jobs to make ends meet,
韦克罗斯的老师为了维持收支平衡而打两份工，

100
00:12:30,530 --> 00:12:36,310
And the student in Albany who told me that she was making choices between rent,
奥尔巴尼的一名学生告诉我，她正在租金之间做出选择，

101
00:12:36,690 --> 00:12:38,270
Food, and her books.
食物，还有她的书。

102
00:12:39,339 --> 00:12:43,550
Our campaign is about Georgians across this state.
我们的活动是关于全州佐治亚人的。

103
00:12:44,010 --> 00:12:50,290
It has been about everyone who wants something better for our future.
它关乎每个人都希望我们的未来有更好的发展。

104
00:12:50,990 --> 00:12:58,950
So, Georgia, I have said over the past few days, "If I were your woman."
所以，佐治亚，我在过去几天里说过，“如果我是你的女人就好了。”

105
00:13:04,400 --> 00:13:06,400
Well, now I am your woman.
好吧，现在我是你的女人了。

106
00:13:07,319 --> 00:13:12,880
And here is what I will do.
这就是我要做的。

107
00:13:13,420 --> 00:13:17,880
I will never, ever, ever stop loving you.
我永远、永远、永远不会停止爱你。

108
00:13:20,604 --> 00:13:26,900
Thank you, Georgia, for electing me as your governor.
佐治亚州，谢谢您选举我担任州长。

109
00:13:27,560 --> 00:13:33,420
God bless you all, and may God bless our great state.
愿上帝保佑你们所有人，愿上帝保佑我们伟大的国家。

110
00:13:33,920 --> 00:13:34,000
Thank you.
谢谢你。
